{
 "esm": "1.0.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "F12cRecurrenceViaADiscreteEvent",
  "description": "FINDING F22 (expected to FAIL). an `update` of kind `discrete` on an array-shaped variable does not evaluate on the array path.\n\nFOUND WHILE LOOKING FOR SOMETHING ELSE, AND IT OUTLIVED IT. This document began as one of four candidate spellings for F12's recurrence. F12 is now fixed by a causal self-reference, so this is no longer a recurrence question -- but the document still fails, and what it fails at is a real and separate gap: a discrete event works on the scalar path and not on the array path. Re-filed as F22 rather than retired with F12, because retiring it would have deleted a live limitation along with the solved one.\n\nNOTHING IN THIS PORT NEEDS IT TODAY. It is recorded so that the next author who reaches for it finds a measurement instead of a surprise. See docs/findings/README.md F22.\n\n--- the original F12 note follows ---\n\nREPRO, EXPECTED TO FAIL, AND SILENTLY. F12's third spelling, and the one F12 rules out on a CONVENTION -- a MOVES calculator carries no clock (PLAN.md \u00a71.2). That reason is sound but it is not the binding one, and this repro records the binding one: even a document that DOES take a clock cannot fold this way, because the Rust array backend does not execute events.\n\n`s` doubles on a `periodic` discrete event of interval 1, from s(0) = 1, so s(3.5) should be 8 -- the same recurrence as F12, run on the time axis with `Pre` instead of over an index axis. The same recurrence F12 asks for -- s[1] = 1, s[k] = 2*s[k-1], answer [1, 2, 4, 8] -- so the four spellings are directly comparable.\n\nThe document validates and the run COMPLETES, reporting s(3.5) = 1: the event never fired and nothing said so. The scalar backend, reached by a document with no array variable, refuses the same file loudly --\n\n    Compile failed: Unsupported feature 'discrete_events': v1 does not support\n    discrete events. Track the future Rust events bead for support.\n\n-- so the silence is specific to the ARRAY path, which is the only path a relational MOVES component can take (docs/esm-conventions.md \u00a72: a component always has at least one array). A `parameter` carrying an `update` of kind `schedule` with a `Pre` expression -- \u00a75.4's replacement for the same construct -- IS refused loudly on the array path: `Unsupported feature 'discrete': ... parameter 'g' carries an `expression` update`. So the one shape of time-axis fold that reaches the array evaluator at all is the one that is dropped without a word.\n\nConsequence for F12's write-up: `Pre` is not merely inconvenient for a calculator with no clock, it is unavailable to any array document whatever its clock. Adopting a clock would not unblock `agedist.f`.",
  "authors": [
   "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
  ],
  "tags": [
   "finding",
   "expected-to-fail",
   "events",
   "recurrence",
   "silent"
  ]
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "step_rows": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 2
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "F12cRecurrenceViaADiscreteEvent": {
   "tolerance": {
    "rel": 1e-12
   },
   "variables": {
    "s": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Doubles at each event; 1 at t = 0."
    },
    "s_seen": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "step_rows"
     ],
     "units": "1",
     "description": "`s` broadcast over an axis, so the document takes the ARRAY path -- which is what makes the event silently vanish rather than be refused."
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "lhs": {
      "op": "D",
      "args": [
       "s"
      ],
      "wrt": "t"
     },
     "rhs": 0.0
    },
    {
     "lhs": {
      "op": "ic",
      "args": [
       "s"
      ]
     },
     "rhs": 1.0
    },
    {
     "lhs": "s_seen",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "args": [],
      "output_idx": [
       "k"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "k": {
        "from": "step_rows"
       }
      },
      "expr": "s"
     }
    }
   ],
   "discrete_events": [
    {
     "name": "double",
     "trigger": {
      "type": "periodic",
      "interval": 1.0
     },
     "affects": [
      {
       "lhs": "s",
       "rhs": {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "Pre",
          "args": [
           "s"
          ]
         },
         2.0
        ]
       }
      }
     ],
     "description": "s := 2*Pre(s), once per unit of time."
    }
   ],
   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "a_periodic_event_folds_an_unknown",
     "description": "INTENDED behaviour: three firings by t = 3.5, so s = 8 and s_seen = 8. Measured: both are 1.",
     "time_span": {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.5
     },
     "assertions": [
      {
       "variable": "s_seen",
       "time": 3.5,
       "expected": 8.0,
       "coords": {
        "step_rows": 1
       }
      },
      {
       "variable": "s",
       "time": 3.5,
       "expected": 8.0
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 }
}